Hallucination in large language models is well documented(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "huang2024hallucination"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 One response is to make models cite their sources:
 Rashkin et al.
 define when generated text is attributable to a source(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "rashkin2023ais"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 Gao et al.
 benchmark the citation quality of LLM answers(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "gao2023alce"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 and Liu et al.
 found that only about half of the sentences produced by generative search engines were fully supported by their citations(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "liu2023verifiability"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 These approaches evaluate citations after the fact,
 usually with human or model judges.
 epistaint instead records the evidence at the moment a tool is called,
 outside the model's control,
 so that citations can be checked deterministically.
 Tracking how information flows between sources of different trust is the idea behind information-flow control(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "denning1976lattice"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 which has recently been applied to LLM agents for security,
 to stop untrusted tool outputs,
 such as indirect prompt injections (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "greshake2023indirect"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 from steering an agent's actions (
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "debenedetti2025camel,costa2025fides"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
 I apply the same idea to epistemics rather than security:
 the labels describe how trustworthy a claim's evidence is.
 The log is hash-chained,
 the classic construction for tamper-evident logs;
 Crosby and Wallach describe a more efficient tree-based alternative(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "crosby2009tamper"
literal "false"

\end_inset

),
 and the proxy wraps the Model Context Protocol(
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "anthropic2024mcp"
literal "false"

\end_inset

).
\begin_inset Separator parbreak
\end_inset


\end_layout

