Epistemic taint tracking does not stop an LLM agent from making unsupported claims,
 but it makes them visible:
 each claim is either tied to the tool output it relies on,
 with a trust tier,
 or flagged.
 In a small evaluation,
 provenance linked up to 92% of an agent's claims to specific evidence and caught every fabricated citation planted in real answers,
 with no false positives.
 Checking whether a cited claim interprets its evidence correctly remains the main open problem.
